 "applies_to": "TSI SureFlow Model 8682-BAC adaptive offset controllers (up to 4 supplies, 2 general exhausts and 7 hoods) with the BACnet MS/TP board.",
 "summary": "The SureFlow 8682 controls a laboratory room by tracking up to four supply, two general exhaust and seven fume hood flows to hold a flow offset, trimming it to a room pressure setpoint, with reheat temperature control. Over BACnet MS/TP it exposes room pressure, every flow and the totals, the current offset, temperature, damper and valve positions, setpoints and alarm limits, occupancy, remote and emergency commands, and a Status Index alarm code.",
 "bacnet_transport": [
  "BACnet MS/TP"
 ],
 "firmware": "1.0 (PICS)",
 "default_device_instance": 868001,
 "access_inferred": true,
 "notes": [
  "From the Model 8682-BAC BACnet MS/TP Object Set table (manual pages 92-93).",
  "The table has no read/write column. Access is inferred from the PICS, which lists Present_Value as writable for Analog, Binary and Multi-state Values only.",
  "Units follow Units Value (MV 3): 1 = ft/min, 2 = m/s, 3 = in. H2O, 4 = Pa; English units (cfm, °F) apply with 1 or 3. English is the default.",
  "Emergency Mode (MV 2) prints only states 1 and 2, unlike the 8681."
 ],
